## MULTIPLE WAYS TWINTHOS/DEWEY HELPS — BY AGENT TYPE

These are the distinct agent capabilities that can be deployed to any of the above industries. Each industry gets a different combination.

### Agent Type 1: Inbox/Communication Triage Agent
**What it does:** Triages incoming communication (email, messages, calls), drafts responses to routine items, flags urgent ones, follows up on unanswered threads, maintains communication logs.
**Deploy to:** Every industry. Law firms (client emails, opposing counsel), insurance (client emails, carrier communications), manufacturers (customer orders, supplier emails), wholesalers (order emails, customer inquiries), real estate (lead emails, client messages), marketing agencies (client emails, platform notifications).
**Pitch:** "Your inbox is costing you decisions. We deploy an AI employee that handles your communication — triaging, drafting, following up — so you only see what needs your attention."

### Agent Type 2: Document/Form Automation Agent
**What it does:** Fills templates from structured data, generates drafts of standard documents, checks for consistency, routes for human review, learns preferences over time.
**Deploy to:** Law firms (engagement letters, pleadings, demand letters, settlement agreements), insurance (renewal proposals, coverage summaries, claim forms, compliance docs), manufacturers (packaging docs, compliance certs, shipping docs), wholesalers (quotes, order confirmations), real estate (transaction documents, listing descriptions, marketing materials), marketing agencies (client reports, campaign briefs, content drafts).
**Pitch:** "You have templates you fill out over and over. We deploy an AI employee that generates those documents from your data — first draft, ready for your review — in seconds, not hours."

### Agent Type 3: Follow-up/Tracking Agent
**What it does:** Tracks every open loop — leads, client questions, colleague requests, deadlines, renewals, follow-ups — and follows up persistently until resolved. Maintains the list. Escalates when needed.
**Deploy to:** Every industry. Law firms (client follow-ups, deadline tracking, colleague coordination), insurance (policy renewal follow-ups, claim status follow-ups, lead follow-ups), manufacturers (order follow-ups, supplier follow-ups, customer inquiries), wholesalers (order follow-ups, customer inquiries, shipping follow-ups), real estate (lead follow-ups, showing follow-ups, transaction milestone follow-ups), marketing agencies (client deliverable follow-ups, campaign milestone tracking).
**Pitch:** "Things fall through the cracks because no one follows up. We deploy an AI employee that tracks every open loop and never misses a follow-up — leads, clients, deadlines, colleagues."

### Agent Type 4: Data Entry/Order Processing Agent
**What it does:** Receives orders, inquiries, requests from multiple channels (email, portal, form, phone), enters them into the system, confirms receipt, flags issues, generates confirmations.
**Deploy to:** Manufacturers (PO entry from email/fax/portal), wholesalers (order entry from all channels), real estate (lead capture from Zillow/website/social), insurance (quote requests, application intake), marketing agencies (lead capture, project request intake).
**Pitch:** "Orders, inquiries, requests come in through email, portals, forms, phone — and someone has to enter them all. We deploy an AI employee that captures and processes every incoming request 24/7 — no more manual data entry."

### Agent Type 5: Reporting/Analytics Agent
**What it does:** Pulls data from multiple systems, compiles into reports, writes narrative summaries, sends to stakeholders, tracks KPIs, flags anomalies.
**Deploy to:** Law firms (time reporting, matter status, financial summaries), insurance (renewal reports, commission summaries, client coverage reports), manufacturers (production reports, quality reports, inventory reports), wholesalers (sales reports, inventory reports, order reports), real estate (market reports, listing performance, transaction status reports), marketing agencies (client reports from multiple platforms — Google Ads, Meta, analytics, SEO).
**Pitch:** "You spend hours every week pulling data from different systems and compiling reports. We deploy an AI employee that generates those reports automatically — data, narrative, delivery — on schedule, every time."

### Agent Type 6: Scheduling/Calendar Agent
**What it does:** Manages calendar, schedules meetings, coordinates availability, sends confirmations and reminders, prepares agendas, cancels/reschedules as needed.
**Deploy to:** Every industry. Law firms (client consultations, court dates, depositions, meetings), insurance (client appointments, renewal meetings, carrier meetings), manufacturers (production meetings, supplier meetings, customer visits), wholesalers (customer appointments, sales meetings), real estate (showings, inspections, closings, client meetings), marketing agencies (client meetings, campaign launches, content calendar).
**Pitch:** "Your calendar is a mess of scheduling back-and-forth, missed confirmations, and forgotten reminders. We deploy an AI employee that manages your calendar end-to-end — scheduling, confirming, reminding, preparing."

### Agent Type 7: Lead Qualification/Response Agent
**What it does:** Captures inbound leads from all sources, qualifies using defined criteria, routes to right person, schedules appointments, sends initial information, follows up persistently.
**Deploy to:** Law firms (intake leads from website, phone, referrals), insurance (quote requests, coverage inquiries, referral leads), manufacturers (RFQ responses, customer inquiries), wholesalers (customer inquiries, quote requests), real estate (internet leads from Zillow/Realtor.com/website, referral leads), marketing agencies (agency's own inbound leads, discovery call scheduling).
**Pitch:** "Leads go cold in hours. You're losing business because no one responds fast enough. We deploy an AI employee that captures every lead, qualifies it, and responds within minutes — 24/7 — so no opportunity slips through."

### Agent Type 8: Inventory/Asset Tracking Agent
**What it does:** Monitors inventory or asset levels across locations, triggers reorders when thresholds hit, tracks shipments, updates records, generates reports, flags anomalies.
**Deploy to:** Manufacturers (raw materials, finished goods, WIP), wholesalers (stock across warehouses/locations), real estate (property availability, listing status), marketing agencies (content calendar, campaign assets).
**Pitch:** "You don't know what's in stock until you check. Stockouts cost you sales. Excess inventory costs you carrying costs. We deploy an AI employee that tracks inventory across all locations and triggers reorders automatically — so you never stock out and never over-order."

