## DEWEY/TWINTHOS SPECIFIC CAPABILITIES

These are the capabilities that make Twinthos/Dewey different from a generic AI automation agency. They come from Nick Vasilescu's architecture and the Orgo/Hermes/Composio stack.

### Capability 1: Computer-use agents (not just API integrations)
Most AI automation agencies build API-based automations (Zapier, Make, N8N). These hit a wall when there's no API, incomplete API, or API requires permissions the user doesn't have.
**Twinthos/Dewey advantage:** Computer-use agents can do anything a human can do in a UI — click, type, scroll, navigate, extract. "Every reason a personal computer is valuable for a human is also a reason for a personal computer being valuable for AI."
**Pitch:** "Other agencies build automations that break when your software doesn't have an API. We deploy AI employees that use your computers the way you do — clicking, typing, navigating — so they work with your existing systems, not against them. No API required."

### Capability 2: Each agent gets its own persistent computer
Most agents run on shared infrastructure. When they break, debugging is hard. When they need different environments, it's messy.
**Twinthos/Dewey advantage:** Each agent gets its own Orgo computer that persists. Agent shuts down to save cost when idle, but computer remains. Agent returns to same state. "The agent should be shut down of course just to save token cost when the task is complete but the computer itself should remain running so that the agent could always return to that same computer whenever the script is run again."
**Pitch:** "Each of your AI employees gets its own computer — persistent, isolated, always ready. When one breaks, the others keep running. When you need to debug, you remote in. No shared infrastructure, no cascading failures."

### Capability 3: Orchestrator + sub-agents architecture
Most agencies build one big automation that tries to do everything. When it breaks, everything breaks. Debugging is a nightmare.
**Twinthos/Dewey advantage:** Orchestrator (named "Hubert" in Nick's setup) stays in charge 99% of the time, hands tasks to specialized sub-agents. "One giant bloated agent is a nightmare to debug. This way everything stays clean and purpose-built."
**Pitch:** "Other agencies build one automation that tries to do everything — when it breaks, everything breaks. We deploy an orchestrator that manages specialized AI employees — intake agent, document agent, follow-up agent — each purpose-built, each debuggable independently."

### Capability 4: Templates — spin up in minutes, not days
Most agencies build each client's automation from scratch. Every engagement is a custom project. Scaling means more people.
**Twinthos/Dewey advantage:** Nick makes a template for each agent he builds and gives them away free. "Spin up an AI employee in minutes, not days." The nicks-stack template includes: Telegram QR onboarding, Composio, AgentPhone SMS, Obsidian, gpt-5.5 — bring your own keys, zero secrets baked in.
**Pitch:** "Other agencies build every client's automation from scratch — that's why they're expensive and slow. We deploy from templates — your AI employee is running in minutes, not weeks. The template handles onboarding, connectors, knowledge base, interface. We customize for your business, not rebuild from zero."

### Capability 5: Demo-first, visual sales
Most agencies sell on presentations, reports, promises. The client has to imagine what it will do.
**Twinthos/Dewey advantage:** Computer use is visual. "When you have a sexy demo, you can convert the client." "Computer use is very visual. You can understand what's going on as a client who has no tech experience. It's very cool to watch." Nick sends clips of the agent working to the client as the demo.
**Pitch:** "Other agencies show you slides and make promises. We show you the AI employee working — clicking through your systems, processing your orders, handling your clients — recorded and sent to you. You see it work before you buy. The demo converts."

### Capability 6: Natural language = the interface
Most agencies require the client to learn tools, workflows, dashboards. The client has to adapt to the automation.
**Twinthos/Dewey advantage:** "If you can describe a process in words and understand the sequence and combination of these different elements involved of a workflow, then you can create a computer use agent for it with natural language." "You don't have to write a single line of code." The client talks to the agent in English (or any language). The agent does the work.
**Pitch:** "Other agencies make you learn their tools, their dashboards, their workflows. We deploy AI employees you talk to in plain English — describe what you need, and it gets done. No new software to learn. No dashboard to master."

### Capability 7: 48-hour delivery
Most agencies take weeks or months to deliver. The client waits. Momentum dies.
**Twinthos/Dewey advantage:** "It shouldn't take longer than 48 hours to get up and running with the first agent for your customer." The template + Orgo + Hermes + Composio stack makes this possible.
**Pitch:** "Other agencies take weeks to deliver. We deploy your first AI employee in 48 hours. You see value in two days, not two months. The clock starts when you say yes."

### Capability 8: Unlimited offering (abundance model)
Most agencies sell scoped projects with limited scope, change orders, usage caps. The client worries about scope creep, extra charges, running out of credits.
**Twinthos/Dewey advantage:** "Unlimited agents, unlimited usage, unlimited monitoring, support, security, ongoing changes, etc." "The point is not that the customer needs infinite agents. They don't need infinite tokens or infinite computers. Most customers they just need one, maybe two, maybe three." The abundance model removes friction from the offer.
**Pitch:** "Other agencies sell you scoped projects with change orders and usage caps. We offer unlimited — unlimited agents, unlimited usage, unlimited support, unlimited changes. You're not worrying about scope creep or running out of credits. You're getting an AI employee that just works."

